      "content": "When designing questions, focus on how individuals react to perceived disrespect or immediate danger, which is a common theme in survival-based social dynamics. For instance, present a scenario where someone cuts you off aggressively in traffic and ask about your immediate, gut reaction—do you ignore it, retaliate immediately, or calmly address it? Another scenario could involve a perceived slight from a stranger, asking if you would escalate the situation or de-escalate it. These questions probe reactive tendencies without explicitly labeling any group.",
